WEBVTT

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.150
Lord Richard.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.900
Catesby.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:14.070
Mother says she'll take me to the woods
today because the weather is fine.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:17.530
Come. Let's go deep into the woods.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.410
Catesby, um...

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.580
If I get lost in the woods,

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.210
come and find me, okay?

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.840
Catesby.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.130
I'll go on alone.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.010
Sweet strawberry pies.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.390
Why not bring one home to your family?

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.690
I have no reason to call on him.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.280
If Richard won't speak against
His Majesty's whims,

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.450
you'll have to rely on the queen mother.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.900
But then...

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:00.740
Asking her for a bit of advice
wouldn't be a betrayal.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:01.660
Don't tell me...

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.670
York of the white rose.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:10.210
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:16.720
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.470
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.780
The next council will decide whether
you take the throne at the coronation.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.240
Who might take our side?

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:08.370
By my reckoning, it's evenly split.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:12.000
The Earl of Northumberland
and Lord Howard are ours.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.540
Hastings and Stanley could be persuaded.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.500
And the Bishop of Ely?

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.090
We can buy his support.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.260
I'll speak to him, then.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.510
I'll meet with Howard
and the others as well.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.810
But what if they won't join us?

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:34.810
No one could refuse your
impassioned whisper in their ear.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.400
And if that fails?

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.940
We'll need to kill them.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:42.950
Otherwise, it will be our heads
on the executioner's block.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:46.490
We've embarked on a game
of chance against God.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.290
If Hastings goes that way,

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.620
what will become of him?

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.460
Of whom?

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.920
Catesby is a loyal man.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:01.590
Will he look at me with hate in his eyes?

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.930
If he truly cares for the
royal family, he'll understand.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:10.770
But if he becomes a briar in our path,

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.230
I'll clear him from it personally.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.780
Mother! He's here!

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:24.530
I see. You've kept me waiting.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.030
Hastings the dolt!

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:33.460
Thank you for your visit, Lord Hastings.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.170
Q-Queen Elizabeth.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.540
I'm sorry that I can't do more for you,

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:43.840
but I now spend my days
praying for a quiet life.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.760
I guarantee your safety
so long as you remain here.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.010
But I was hoping you'd advise me.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:56.020
Goodness. Do you need
advice from the likes of me?

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:01.780
To earnestly seek knowledge from
your enemy shows nobility of spirit.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:06.990
Lord Hastings, a man like
you should be Protector!

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.870
Y-You give me too much credit.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:14.040
No. I could safely entrust
Edward to <i>your</i> care.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.920
Should I report to His Grace?

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.630
But if the Duke of Buckingham
learned of this...

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:28.260
Where are you bound for, Lord Hastings?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.810
An abbey is hardly a fitting place
to rendezvous with a lover,

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:36.180
although it would suit an interview
with the queen dowager.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.480
She's had a complete change of heart!

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.860
You needn't fear her designs on--

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.730
Your Grace!

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.900
I wish to make a statement.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:50.870
Lord Hastings acts with the interests
of the royal family at heart.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:55.370
Punish me if I speak falsely.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:06:00.540
I see. In that case, I wish to speak
with you in your master's stead.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.540
Come.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.880
Why did you shield Hastings?

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.430
Is your wish to remain pure until death?

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.390
Whom do you serve?

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.720
My master is...

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.810
Do you think you
understand him best of all?

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.980
Kindness isn't what he desires now.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.360
You can't become a demon.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.110
You can't save Richard.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:40.500
You met with the Bishop of Ely.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.290
Were you able to buy him off?

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.670
Wait!

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.960
What is this mark?!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.970
It appears the bishop has immoral tastes.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:55.350
He asked for my body rather than gold.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:58.230
Did he defile you?

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:01.480
I'll gouge out his guts
and tear him apart!

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.940
What is there to be upset about?

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:07.610
This won us the bishop's support.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.320
Why are you angry? Tell me.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.530
Our oath.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.080
I haven't broken it.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.160
This body will not open to anyone but you.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.840
Thank you for earlier!

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.420
You're the purest and most
upstanding man I've ever seen.

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.300
Whom do you serve?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.890
You can't save Richard.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.270
Your Grace.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.020
Catesby?

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.940
I wish to speak to you.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.360
I can't just now.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.940
I don't mind. Come in.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.660
It's about Lord Hastings.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.410
Pardon me.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:04.370
If he becomes a briar...

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:08.040
If you turn your sword on me, then...

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:19.720
Lord Hastings often meets the queen
dowager secretly at Westminster.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:24.020
I'm certain that their ties
are strengthening.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:28.150
And what do you intend
to do about Hastings?

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:33.490
If he shows signs of treachery,

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:36.320
I'll dispatch him at once.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:41.500
Your master is loyal to
the royal family, while I...

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:47.000
I am about to betray even the
blood of York to gain the crown.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:53.050
I have only ever served a single lord.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:55.760
Only you, Your Grace.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:03.060
I'm a demon. Consigning you
to hell gives me relief

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:07.480
as you look at me in pain,
bound by your loyalty.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:15.490
Then from now on, consider my orders
as Richard's. We're halves of one whole.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:18.410
Yes, Your Grace.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:22.790
In that case, would you
begin by lopping off

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.410
that traitor's head?

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.670
His blood will seal our compact.

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:37.130
This warmth burns me.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:40.550
Nothing is as vivid as this warmth.

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.140
Your Grace, allow me.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:47.600
I'm about to meet with Lord Howard
and others at a tournament.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.150
They're strongly behind us, but...

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:53.070
Will they still consent
to back you as king?

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.740
I'll have them forge a pact as well.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.070
D-Duke of Gloucester!

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:02.830
Bishop of Ely. What is it?

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.700
I-I must tell you...

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.370
Then you may speak to me.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.620
But it is a private matter.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.540
No matter. Proceed.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:20.180
You see... a service is planned for the
queen mother and her son, Edward V.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.720
A church service?!

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.430
I've heard nothing of this.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.020
You were not meant to.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.390
The archbishop proposed it,

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:33.570
but the queen dowager worked through
Lord Hastings to request it of him.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.400
Good day, Duke of Gloucester.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:39.070
Please visit to sample my strawberries
whenever it pleases you.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:44.080
This proves Hastings a traitor.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.750
Still, I hadn't expected
Elizabeth to be so bold.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.120
Holding this service

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:55.130
will demonstrate that the queen
dowager still wields great power.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.920
But if we prevent it,

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:01.300
we'll suffer a fatal backlash as
enemies of the poor widowed queen.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:05.220
This is a declaration of war from God

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.640
against the devil.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:11.140
The devil has the devil's way.

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:18.030
I thought it a sin even to wish
for warmth, but now it is mine.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:21.530
I'll take what I desire by force.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:29.580
Lord Hastings, has the date
of the service been set?

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:33.750
Actually, the service has been canceled.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:39.340
And what's more, there's to be a service
for the Duke of Gloucester instead.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.630
Impossible!

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.300
Who gave the order?!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.340
It was a royal decree.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.470
Richard must have talked the king into it.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:49.930
That demon!

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:53.190
Frankly, given his current position,

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.820
he might issue royal orders
without the king's knowledge.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:00.940
Also, um... I hate to say this,

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:05.990
but the Duke of Gloucester
demands the younger prince as well.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.410
Queen Elizabeth...

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.000
That demon gives no quarter!

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:18.290
Does he plan to take all my
hopes and leave me in despair?

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:21.920
But I've devoted my life to revenge.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:25.930
The more he takes,
the hotter my soul burns.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.930
Just you watch, Richard.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:31.730
Next time, I'll be the one
to dash your hopes.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.640
Mother.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:37.230
Of course. Why didn't I realize?

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:43.400
Who knows--and hates--Richard most of all?

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:44.240
Your Majesty!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:50.120
The Duke of Gloucester's actions clearly
overstep his authority as Protector!

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:53.160
True. He has been a bit
highhanded of late.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.370
Don't you agree, Your Excellency?

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.830
A-Absolutely.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:01.760
Yes! He's far too impudent!
Far too tyrannical!

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.300
Wait, Lord Hastings!

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:05.760
Lord Howard.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.430
It's cowardly to speak
thus in his absence!

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:13.270
His Majesty formally delegated his
power to the Duke of Gloucester.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:14.930
It is you who are impudent!

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:18.480
Mere excuses!
It's obvious who is in the right!

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.480
A mother's purehearted--

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:21.320
Hastings!

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:23.780
Church services are dull.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:25.990
--But Your Majesty--
--Leave us.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:32.120
--They say Hastings is sleeping
with the queen mother.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:32.120
--First the witch and now the wife? --He must want to be the king's father.

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:35.210
I realized too late.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:39.290
The palace is already
full of rotten apples.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:42.380
The few of us left must
talk amongst ourselves.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.550
I know just the place!

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.930
May God bless you, guardians of justice.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:52.180
Lord Stanley. Lord Hastings.
Bishop of Ely.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.560
The royal family is doomed

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:58.810
unless we seize England back
from that lawless fiend, Richard!

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:02.480
But our situation is even
more dire than before.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:05.610
Richard was a reserved
and straightforward soldier.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:08.950
Now, he has a strange
power to attract people.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.990
It's practically magical!

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:15.160
Wealth and power cast a potent spell.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:17.500
Qu-Quite right!

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:22.340
If only we knew his secret weakness.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:25.880
Some scandal that would
shake people's faith in him.

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:29.590
I take it that's why
you called, Elizabeth.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:31.300
Why you summoned me!

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.680
Mother-in-law!

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.640
Please forgive my abrupt summons.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.890
God has left this task to us.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:42.900
Elizabeth, I understand.
Your sorrow is my own,

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:47.320
although my sorrow is many times greater.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:54.120
But the fruit of my womb and his
wickedness lies behind it all.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:58.450
In exchange for my aid,
I want you to promise me one thing:

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.420
Kill Richard.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.880
I've tried many times myself,
but I couldn't do it.

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:11.340
Oh! If only I could have
slain him with words!

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:16.930
I should have exposed Richard's secret
and let the world punish him sooner!

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.220
What secret?

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:24.020
I concealed it because it could have
brought ruin on our house.

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.440
And in consequence,

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:31.360
my cowardice has allowed
that demon to flourish!

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:34.820
But now I have no more left to lose.

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:38.200
Nothing but my dear Edward's children.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:39.620
Yes, precisely!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.710
For those darling children's sakes,

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:45.340
tell us the truth about Richard now!

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:48.170
Richard Plantagenet is...

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:57.640
A blood-soaked demon
who defied the will of God!

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:58.770
Let me prophecy!

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:04.100
One day, a host of the elderly,
of widows, of orphans

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:08.270
will lament the untimely
deaths that demon caused!

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:09.230
What did he say?

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:10.190
Duke Richard is...?

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:14.200
This will let us strike a fatal
blow against Gloucester,

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.950
although it is quite hard to believe.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:22.580
No, thinking back, his actions
were always strange.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:27.750
It all makes sense. We shall indict
him at the next council meeting

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:32.010
and expose his true demonic
nature to the light of day!

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.630
Why was he born?

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.340
Why was he ever born?!

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:37.220
Curse the day of his birth!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.760
Curse the demon!

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:41.720
The demon, Richard Plantagenet!

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:49.440
What a racket.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:53.700
He must want the next council
to have you burned at the stake.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.910
Is that your idea of informing?

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.830
It's too late to beg for your life.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:03.290
I knew His Grace's secret,
but I didn't tell it.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:07.460
But do you truly understand yourself?

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:09.790
Have you felt at all unusual?

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:13.590
If you have need of medicines,
just say the word.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:16.220
That potion that sapped the king's will?

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:18.010
An abortifacient.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:23.180
Take care. It causes
inflammation in sunlight.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:30.060
It won't be a demon on display
at the next council meeting.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.650
It will be his head.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.280
Where is the rest of the council?

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:41.830
Oh, we must have arrived too early.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:44.870
Even the Duke of Gloucester
isn't here yet.

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:50.250
Can't you stand in for him?

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:53.420
You know his mind better than anyone.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:59.180
Me? We may be close friends,
but I can't fathom his innermost thoughts.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:02.850
Just as you and I cannot
know each other's minds.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:07.020
Pardon my tardiness, my lords.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:13.940
Now, what shall we discuss?

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:15.940
Why, the coronation, of--

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:18.280
By the way, Your Excellency,

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:21.780
was that not an intimate time
we spent the other day?

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:22.990
Just us two.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:28.710
You promised to send me
strawberries from your garden.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.920
Would you go and fetch them now?

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.630
N-Now?

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:33.750
Yes, now.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:36.550
E-Excuse me.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.010
Now, what date shall we set?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.720
The others are too late.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.430
Duke of Gloucester,

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:46.810
may I step out for a moment as well?

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:47.810
By all means.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:54.820
Lord Hastings,

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:59.200
the other councilors have
convened in another location.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:02.780
Damn! So, Gloucester <i>has</i> bought them off.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:06.950
Catesby! Gather as many
of the nobles here as you can!

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:08.910
They can witness the charges!

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.420
As for that, they are already here.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:17.760
Incredible. You're the most
capable and loyal man I know.

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:24.470
Gloucester is your former lord,
so I'm sure your feelings are conflicted.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:31.060
I merely wished for His Grace
to walk in the warm light.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:36.860
You should at least be
the one to end his misery.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:45.070
Duke of Gloucester! Let me tell you
the <i>true</i> purpose of this council!

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:49.910
Listen well! Richard Plantagenet
schemes to overthrow the kingdom!

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:56.340
His mother, Duchess Cecily, has revealed
the truth, heedless of her own dishonor!

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:59.960
Richard harbors a demon in his flesh!

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:08.430
Richard! If you claim innocence,
then present proofs!

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:10.020
Here and now!

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:14.310
A cursed demon, am I?

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.520
And who cursed me?

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:23.530
My body has been twisted into
this ghastly, demonic form.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:27.780
Are not those who cast that
curse the <i>true</i> demons?

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:31.790
Hastings and his allies!

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.660
You are the demons!

00:20:33.660 --> 00:20:35.710
Y-You lie!

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.340
Then behold.

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:43.170
I was not born this way.

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:49.260
This is the result of your curse.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:51.180
Put these rebels to death!

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:57.150
Now I'm certain of everything,
even without proof!

00:20:57.150 --> 00:21:00.730
You fools seek the empty favor of a demon!

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.240
Catesby! Seize Richard!

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:09.700
That day, I could not save him.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:12.410
Lord Richard! Lord Richard!

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:15.330
What shall I do? If Lord Richard is...

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:16.790
Your Grace,

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:21.340
I can never become the light
that illumines your path.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:22.590
Even so...

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:29.100
...to me, you are life itself.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.600
Lord Hastings, prepare yourself.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.770
Even you?!

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:39.810
Disgusting! I would rather die
than see a demon crowned!

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:43.690
Even so, I will never leave you alone.

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:48.160
No matter how deep into
darkness your path takes you.
